title: config get renders hash-form statuses as HASH(0x...)
updated: 2026-08-11T19:33:48Z
---

karr config get statuses prints:

    backlog, todo, HASH(0x558580cd1688), HASH(0x558582ac9348), done, archived

The default status list (Config.pm:681-688) mixes plain strings with hashes:
in-progress and review carry require_claim => 1, so they are HASH refs, and the
scalar-joining renderer in config get stringifies the ref instead of its name.

Same shape is likely reachable for priorities and classes, which also allow the
hash form (classes are hashes throughout: wip_limit, bypass_column_wip).

Not cosmetic: the output is what a reader consults to learn which columns a
board has. Two unreadable entries invite invention. This was found after an
agent claimed one board had an "extended status set" including a closed status
that no board in the tree actually configures -- every board runs the defaults.

Expected: print the status name, and ideally its per-status settings in a form
that survives --json too. Config->statuses already normalises to names
(Config.pm:100-104); config get is not using it.
Fixed: config get/show now render list entries as name plus per-entry settings (Cmd/Config.pm _format_entry/_format_settings); --json unchanged (already faithful). Regression test t/129-config-list-entry-rendering.t (RED before fix: 4/7 subtests). Verified: prove -l t/02-config.t t/06-config-cmd.t t/49-config-skill-options-first.t t/53-config-semantics.t t/64-disable-enable-cmd.t t/94-write-path-validation.t t/102-import-config-reconcile.t t/129-config-list-entry-rendering.t -> PASS; prove -l t/ -> Files=121, Tests=848, Result: PASS. Not committed.
